WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.806
- All right, y'all,
let's dip into the world

00:00:01.806 --> 00:00:03.600
of social media before we say goodbye.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.634
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:07.320
(rock music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.270
A woman in southern California woke up

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:12.150
to her dog barking and
scratching at the floor.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.980
She looked outside and noticed the cover

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.170
to her crawlspace ripped off.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.711
When she went to investigate,
she discovered this.

00:00:19.711 --> 00:00:20.820
(audience gasps)

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.530
It's a bear.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.990
A several hundred pound black bear

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.045
just chilling under her
floorboards, hanging out.

00:00:27.045 --> 00:00:30.390
Most of us would freak
out, but not this lady.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.910
She managed to get the
bear out on her own.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:33.743
How did she do it?

00:00:33.743 --> 00:00:35.520
Let's find out for anyone else

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.410
who this happens to.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:38.760
We have Tina on the line,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.530
who watches on NBC Los Angeles.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:41.670
What's up, Tina?

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.443
- Hi, Kelly.
- Hello.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:49.200
What did you do when you
found out it was a bear?

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.130
- I was so nervous when I saw
those eyes staring back at me.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.630
You know, I live in a small suburb

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.520
of Los Angeles County called Monrovia,

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.170
and we get bears all the time.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.300
So, I went back to bed
thinking no big deal.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.340
But when my dog, Archie, went nuts,

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.100
I thought, "Is that bear
underneath my house?"

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.950
When I saw the crawlspace
grate ripped off its hinges,

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.440
I'm like, "Oh no, it's down there."

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.890
So, I walked down to my
basement with my flashlight

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.680
and the eyes shone right back at me.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.330
I thought, "Oh no."

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:19.323
- What did you do?

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:24.115
- Well, I googled, "How to
get a bear out of crawlspace."

00:01:24.115 --> 00:01:26.146
(audience laughing)

00:01:26.146 --> 00:01:28.058
Nothing came up.

00:01:28.058 --> 00:01:29.250
Nothing came up.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.210
So, I thought, well, I'm gonna have

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:31.800
to take this in my own hands.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:35.700
So, I turned my heater on real
high, made a bunch of noise.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:39.150
I got some pots and pans
and started banging them.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.020
It didn't budge.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.280
I got my leaf blower.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.860
I went down there and aimed it at him.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:44.693
It didn't budge.

00:01:44.693 --> 00:01:46.290
It was just laying there looking at me,

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:49.110
blinking at me with those cute eyes.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:51.619
- Oh my god, God bless Google.

00:01:51.619 --> 00:01:53.070
(Tina laughs)

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.570
How'd you finally get the bear out?

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:56.250
- Well, I reached out to our mayor

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.570
who had the police come by,

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:01.650
and they had a public safety
officer who knew about bears,

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:04.057
and he told me, "Get some moth balls

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:06.600
"and throw it up in your crawl space."

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.730
So I did, and it did the trick.

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.340
They don't like the smell of moth balls.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.510
And that bear left.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:14.370
- [Tina] I didn't want a bear sleepover.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.260
- Yeah, that's a big black bear.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.340
He is full.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.590
Yeah, he's not skinny.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.330
Well, thank you so much, Tina.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.490
This is hilarious and I'm
liking your post right now.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.859
I'm glad everything's okay.

00:02:24.859 --> 00:02:26.490
(audience clapping)
(bell dings)

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.836
That picture, man, come
on, can't get over it.

00:02:28.836 --> 00:02:31.230
Our season long partner, Pilot pen,

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:32.820
makers of Precise, the go-to pen

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:33.810
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.640
love your story as much as we do,

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.920
so they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.101
So, maybe invest in some more moth balls.

00:02:40.101 --> 00:02:42.705
(audience cheering)

00:02:42.705 --> 00:02:46.004
All right, thank you, Tina, stay safe.

00:02:46.004 --> 00:02:47.635
And thank you all our guests this hour,

00:02:47.635 --> 00:02:50.392
Kathryn Newton, Cole
Sprouse, Zelda Williams,

00:02:50.392 --> 00:02:52.574
Diablo Cody, Sarah J. Maas,

00:02:52.574 --> 00:02:54.099
and the cast of "Kimberly Akimbo."

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:56.482
Y'all have a great day and
if it's not, change it.

